-- **sccache cache-key sensitivity (frozen iteration profile).** sccache + cargo's per-crate cache key includes `RUSTFLAGS`, `CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO`, and `CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_CODEGEN_UNITS`. Changing any of those between iterations invalidates every cached `rustc` invocation — the next build is effectively cold (~30-60 min of recompile on this workspace). `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS` is NOT in the cache key (pure scheduler input) — it's safe to tune freely. The final binary link step (`codex-core.exe`) is uncacheable regardless of sccache because sccache skips `bin`/`dylib`/`cdylib`/`proc-macro` crates by design; the only lever for link-step wall-time on iteration is `LTO=off` (~30 sec) vs `LTO=thin` (~20 min) vs `LTO=fat` (hours). **Trapdoor — sccache wrapper bypass under LTO!=off:** beyond the cache-key invalidation above, sccache's Rust support inspects the `rustc` command line and BYPASSES caching at the wrapper level whenever `-Clto` is set (any non-off LTO value), shelling straight through to `rustc` without contacting the sccache server. That means switching to `LTO=thin` (or `fat`) loses sccache acceleration on every future build under that profile, not just the first one — the cache is irrelevant because the wrapper never queries it. `LTO=off` is the only profile under which sccache actually wraps `rustc` on this workspace. F-1 in `.ralph/jobs/codex-rs-build-perf-baseline-measurement/benchmark-results.md` (2026-06-01) measured this empirically: the `lto-change` scenario recompiled 939 crates over 57m 57s and logged **0 sccache compile requests / 0 hits / 0 misses / 0 stores**. Source `scripts/iteration-env.sh` to pin the right values; if you genuinely need to test a different profile, version the cache by clearing `D:\codex-sccache` first and document the new profile in `docs/implementation/build-perf.md`. The r6 (2026-05-31) retrospective burned a 2h 47m cold rebuild on this exact pattern — `LTO=thin→off` mid-day forced a wholesale cache invalidation. See `.claude/commands/publish-sandbox-patch.md` Step 2a for the authoritative frozen env block, and `docs/implementation/build-perf.md` § "sccache + LTO interaction" for the wrapper-bypass detail.
