 - **Windows tool-exec children are confined in a Job Object** (v0.121.0-copilot-api.6+). `core/src/spawn.rs::spawn_child_async` spawns `CREATE_SUSPENDED`, assigns to a kill-on-close job, resumes, then installs a watcher that closes the job when the immediate child exits. Without this, grandchildren (cargo/rustc/link.exe) keep inherited pipe handles open, which wedges `BlockingPool::Drop` at shutdown and hangs `codex-core.exe` indefinitely. Helpers in `core/src/windows_job.rs`. Direct `tokio::process::Command::spawn` call sites outside `spawn_child_async` (e.g., `js_repl`, `utils/pty/pipe.rs`) bypass this and risk reintroducing the hang.
 - Set `CODEX_SHUTDOWN_TRACE=1` to print breadcrumbs (`[shutdown-trace] ...` on stderr) through the shutdown path in `exec` and `arg0`. Silent by default. Use to localize a hang to a specific `.await` when diagnosing regressions. **As of v0.129 the `app-server::thread_unsubscribe` breadcrumbs are gone** — they lived in the deleted `app-server/src/codex_message_processor.rs` monolith and were not re-ported (diagnostic-only). The env var is still parsed but currently emits nothing from the app-server side; re-add to `app-server/src/request_processors/thread_processor.rs::thread_unsubscribe_response_inner` if a post-completion hang reappears. **As of the stream-cut diagnostics ship (2026-06-01)**, `CODEX_SHUTDOWN_TRACE=1` also emits `[shutdown-trace] copilot-job-object watcher-installed pid=N` from `spawn.rs::attach_windows_job` and `[shutdown-trace] copilot-job-object close child_handle_addr=0x… job_handle_addr=0x…` from `windows_job.rs::close_job_on_child_exit`. Together the two breadcrumbs distinguish "watcher never installed" vs "watcher installed but never fired" vs "watcher fired and job closed" when diagnosing tool-exec shutdown hangs.
 - **Opt-in stream-cut diagnostics** (`CODEX_STREAM_TRACE=1`, default off; zero overhead when off). The overlay crate `codex-rs-overlay/codex-stream-diagnostics/` wraps the main SSE consumer loop in `core/src/session/turn.rs::try_run_sampling_request` (the `loop { ... match stream.next() ... }` block) so every Copilot SSE turn emits a `[copilot-stream-end]` tracing event with metadata-only fields and, on abnormal termination, a JSONL sidecar at `~/.codex/sessions/<id>/stream-cut-dump.jsonl`. Use to distinguish the "silent end" symptom (`cause = "eof-before-completed"` — `stream.next()` returned `None` before any `ResponseEvent::Completed`) from a clean end (`cause = "completed"`), a provider error (`cause = "provider-error"`), a cancellation (`cause = "client-cancel"`), or a forgotten finalize site (`cause = "unfinalized"` — programming error, not stream cut). **HARD PRIVACY CONSTRAINT:** the diagnostics output is metadata-only (variant names, byte counts, sequence numbers, timestamps, hashed IDs). NEVER customer data — no event payload text, no tool args, no reasoning content. The runtime privacy canary in `codex-rs-overlay/codex-stream-diagnostics/tests/privacy_canary.rs` is a HARD build gate enforcing this; `cargo test -p codex-stream-diagnostics` is the verification command. See `docs/implementation/patch-surface.md` §14 invariant 30 + §15 "Stream-cut diagnostics replant" for the SANDBOX PATCH inventory and rebase recipe.
