+## v0.141.0-copilot-api.3 V2 handoff and exact-wait regressions (2026-07-14)
+
+Introduced in `v0.141.0-copilot-api.3`; fixed in the
+`v0.141.0-copilot-api.4` source candidate. Publication and installation of
+`.4` remain lead/operator-owned.
+
+- **Opaque Copilot child handoff:** MultiAgentV2 exposed `encrypted_content`
+  schemas and always constructed encrypted `agent_message` payloads even though
+  the Copilot Responses transport cannot supply the provider-native encrypted
+  handoff token. Copilot children therefore received opaque/unusable handoff
+  input. `.4` adds the general
+  `ProviderCapabilities::encrypted_inter_agent_messages` capability, defaults
+  capable providers to encrypted behavior, explicitly marks Copilot plaintext,
+  and derives one encoding for spawn/send/follow-up schema plus runtime
+  construction. V1 and encryption-capable providers remain unchanged.
+- **Already-final exact wait:** V2 `wait_agent` only waited on aggregate mailbox
+  activity and had no exact target. A child that reached a final state before
+  the wait started could leave the parent waiting until timeout. `.4` adds the
+  optional `task_name` branch and subscribes to the target's Tokio status watch
+  before reading its current value, covering completion before setup, during
+  setup, and afterward without a check/subscribe gap. Targetless V2 behavior is
+  unchanged.
+- **Required evidence:** retain the focused provider-schema/runtime tests, the
+  focused exact-wait tests (already-final, future final, unrelated completion,
+  steering, timeout, invalid target, and closed status),
+  `just test -p codex-invariant-tests --test multi_agent_v2_handoff`,
+  `bash scripts/audit_invariants.sh`, and
+  `bash scripts/audit_network_calls.sh`. Release acceptance additionally needs
+  the installed `.4` four-role Ralph 5.64 dogfood; source/unit evidence alone
+  is not permission to declare the rollout complete.
+- **Immutable `.3` rollback pins:** GitHub Release/tag
+  `v0.141.0-copilot-api.3`; asset
+  `codex-0.141.0-copilot-api.3-win32-x64.tgz`, byte length `124405641`, SHA-256
+  `29bd5320fac1c2025cffdc85cedaadb6a7f21a93f42ae93dd95e1a1460c5cfbc`;
+  wrapper annotated-tag object `4519c324b1eda33c72bc87e85f76fda01664b14b`
+  peeled to `05e19f09b62a23c382cf564c05ab56cd4d5f3ef2`; nested retention-tag object
+  `0f3d96993cc032c49973114dca0de6c94941dcff` peeled to
+  `35e64ccd74d60c69fd79756d8d6a6c13e3a78254`. Never move either immutable tag.
+- **Containment and rollback:** before `.4`, or if `.4` must be withdrawn,
+  disable V2 per invocation with `-c features.multi_agent_v2=false` or
+  persist `[features] multi_agent = true` and `multi_agent_v2 = false` in
+  `~/.codex/config.toml`. A reinstall of `.3` is permitted only after the exact
+  asset byte length and SHA-256 above verify; then confirm the four Codex
+  binaries plus `rg.exe`, exact `.3` version, path resolution, and a V1
+  spawn/wait/close canary.
+- **Forward-fix policy:** do not delete, overwrite, or relabel `.3` failure
+  evidence and do not move `.3` tags. Before release, revert the candidate
+  commits normally. After release, publish a new `.5` (or later) forward fix;
+  never rebuild `.4` or mutate its release asset in place.
